    {
      "check": "reconcile",
      "difference": -4700,
      "source_page": 7,
      "note": "Cash flow statement total column prints ending cash 36,855,121 and increase 8,881,868, but the fund columns (and the composition of cash lines) add to 36,859,821 / 8,886,568; difference 4,700 equals the Sewer grant."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "GAAP city, FY ending 9/30/2025. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the governmental funds Statement of Revenues, Expenditures (p4, Total Governmental Funds column); balances reconcile (64,936,067 - 8,204,080 + 3,601,759 = 60,333,746). Other financing: loan proceeds 63,739 -> debt_proceeds; insurance recoveries 51,769 -> other_financing. ending_cash = cash and cash equivalents on governmental funds balance sheet (p3); County treasurer cash 288,736 and investments 18,826,145 are separate lines, not included in ending_cash; investments recorded in ending_investments for information. Business-type from proprietary funds statement (p6, Total enterprise column, Electric/Water/Sewer/Gas; Internal Service excluded). Business net position rolls: 233,000,327 + (receipts 100,015,941 - disbursements 84,801,758 = 15,214,183) + other financing 285,145 (contributed capital 422,175 less cost recovered 137,030) - transfers net 3,486,251 - restatement 1,534,815 = 243,478,589. Gain(loss) on sale of assets (315,871) recorded as negative receipt. No single printed total for business-type receipts/disbursements; computed from operating plus nonoperating lines. Business-type depreciation and amortization 11,711,723 and the 'Cash flows' items are on p6/p7; p8 (gained in v7 re-trim) is the cash flow statement's reconciliation of operating income and supplemental information, no new figures needed. Proprietary cash flows from p7 total column (Enterprise funds). Transfers cross-check: governmental in 11,483,611 and out 7,997,360 (net +3,486,251) equals business-type net transfers out (1,203,674 in less 4,689,925 out = -3,486,251); total in 12,687,285 equals total out 12,687,285. Sales Tax out 5,875,555, ARP out 581,789 (matches Sewer transfer in 581,789) etc.; no transfers are hidden inside spending lines, budget schedule spending equals statement totals. Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p9), Street (p10), Sales Tax (p11) and nonmajor combining (p12). The p12 combining page shows only six nonmajor fund columns (Airport, Enhanced & Wireless 911, Drug Task Force, American Rescue Plan, Transit Lines, Special Projects) plus the Total Non-Major column; the other nonmajor funds are on a page not trimmed, so the six do not add to the total. Per the more-than-6-columns rule, detail records the Total Non-Major Governmental Funds column (fund 'Nonmajor funds (combined)') for revenue, expenditure and other financing, and the per-fund lines were removed. Budget-schedule General Fund actuals (budgetary basis, e.g. property 6,235,319) differ from the GAAP statement (6,311,195); both recorded as printed. No business-type (utility) budget schedules are in the trimmed PDF, so detail has no business-type lines. Balance sheet from government-wide Statement of Net Position, Total column (p1). Classification notes: Business tax -> occupation/franchise tax; Intergovernmental in budget schedules -> other state aid (source not itemized). Read pages 1-12 of 12"
}